<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.6.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01356</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.6.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4028ae2a-f4dc-4729-99a9-77299f73f7d0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para id="para-00002">Use the following passage to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
<para id="para-00003">In a newly formed swamp, it is estimated that there are 500 mosquitoes. The population is estimated to double each
  day.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="_43fa5526-480c-4a1a-b106-126d453a95ff" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00004">Let <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represent the total population of mosquitoes and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represent the number of days that have
          passed since the first estimate. What is the equation that represents the growth of the mosquito population?
      </para>
      <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00009"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00010">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.
    </para><para id="para-00011">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_33b363a9-61f9-4568-9026-babbd59ea1e4" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00012">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> represent in this context?</para>
      <para id="para-00013">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00014">This represents 2 days before the first estimate was taken.</para><para id="para-00015">This represents the day before the first estimate was taken.</para><para id="para-00016">This represents the day the first estimate was taken.</para><para id="para-00017">This represents 2 days after the first estimate was taken.</para></problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00018">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.</para><para id="para-00019">The correct answer is 2 days before the first estimate was taken.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a3bf1633-9c98-468d-96b9-797888d0cabe" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00020">What is the estimated number of mosquitoes that were in the new swamp 1 day before the estimate was taken?
      </para>
      <para id="para-00021">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00022">500</para><para id="para-00023">250</para><para id="para-00024">1,000</para><para id="para-00025">125</para></problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.
    </para><para id="para-00027">The correct answer is 250.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="ad3dba8a-cb99-4c43-896e-7877ea939f47" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00028">Use the following passage to answer questions 4 – 6.</para><para id="para-00029">A desert pond is slowly drying up. The average volume of the pond is shown in the table. The first year it was
        measured, the average volume was determined to be 40,000 liters. Double click on mathematical
        expression/equation to enlarge.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, years</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, volume (liters)</emphasis></entry></row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              –4
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              –2
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              40,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              20,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5,000
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
      <para id="para-00030">Which equation represents the pond’s water loss?</para>
      <para id="para-00031">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00032"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00033"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00034"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00035"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00036">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.</para><para id="para-00037">The correct answer is
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_1aa16586-e2a9-4f03-81ba-c6cefedf6bc6" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00038">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> represent in this context?</para>
      <para id="para-00039">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00040">the time it took for the pond to shrink by a factor of 2</para><para id="para-00041">the first time the volume was measured</para><para id="para-00042">the time 2 years after the first time the volume was measured</para><para id="para-00043">the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured</para></problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00044">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.
    </para><para id="para-00045">The correct answer is the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_0523a23f-0076-4431-b856-a144c4d029a5" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00046">What was the average volume of the pond 4 years before the first time the volume was measured?</para>
      <para id="para-00047">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00048">320,000 liters</para><para id="para-00049">160,000 liters</para><para id="para-00050">80,000 liters</para><para id="para-00051">640,000 liters</para></problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00052">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.
    </para><para id="para-00053">The correct answer is 640,000 liters.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="f289d931-83cb-4e3b-adad-e0ecce980124" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00054">Which of the following is equivalent to 6,350,000 in scientific notation?</para>
      <para id="para-00055">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00056"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6.35</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00057"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6.35</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00058"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6.35</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00059"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6.35</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.
    </para><para id="para-00061">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>6.35</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_9de6da24-490a-47d4-a381-5749a1a2ba48" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00062">Which of the following is equivalent to 0.00032 in scientific notation?</para>
      <para id="para-00063">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00064"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00065"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00066"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00067"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00068">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.
    </para><para id="para-00069">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_643511df-673b-4103-a6a5-761446059723" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00070">Which of the following is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>7.24</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> in decimal form?</para>
      <para id="para-00071">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00072">7,240</para><para id="para-00073">724</para><para id="para-00074">72,400</para><para id="para-00075">724,000</para></problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00076">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.</para><para id="para-00077">The correct answer is 7,240.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_31765884-975f-46fe-b3d1-76599c96e5d4" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00078">Which of the following is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5.47</m:mn><m:mi>×</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> in decimal form?</para>
      <para id="para-00079">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00080">0.00547</para><para id="para-00081">0.0000547</para><para id="para-00082">0.00000547</para><para id="para-00083">0.000547</para></problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00084">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.</para><para id="para-00085">The correct answer is 0.0000547.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a543be8b-3931-41cd-87a0-e0cb9643cf50" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00011"><para id="para-00086">Which of the following correctly orders these values from greatest to least?
          
          <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
            <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value R</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  0.00161
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value S</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  \(6.35\times 10^{-3}\)
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value T</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  0.000541
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis>Value U</emphasis></entry><entry>
                  \(7.23\times 10^{-4}\)
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody></tgroup></table>
      </para>
      <para id="para-00087">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00088">Value S, Value R, Value T, Value U</para><para id="para-00089">Value R, Value S, Value T, Value U</para><para id="para-00090">Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T</para><para id="para-00091">Value R, Value S, Value U, Value T</para></problem><solution id="sol-00011"><para id="para-00092">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.5.
    </para><para id="para-00093">The correct answer is Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T.
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content></document>
